clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T18:03:27Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T18:03:27Z","body":"> I've tested the ETC1S encoder, while it transcodes much faster to S3TC/ETC2, the import times become 5-6x as long compared to UASTC. This is really bad, given as the low-quality option is supposed to be the default\n\nBrutal. Thanks for checking. Maybe there is nothing we can do to improve the situation. Transcoding UASTC to etc2/s3tc I think is a non-starter given that it ends up compressing at load time. If ETC1S is really that slow, then it is going to be a significant change. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4634176847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]